<title>FRANCE: French M3 money supply fell 0.4 pct in Sept.</title>
<headline>French M3 money supply fell 0.4 pct in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of France gave the following money supply figures (the year-on-year change is expressed as an average centred on the previous month)</p>
<p> Money measure  Billions   Monthly change    12-month change</p>
<p>(end-Sept)     (unadj)	(adjusted)	   Sept     Aug</p>
<p>    M1	    1,675.0	  0.5		 5.5	6.1</p>
<p>    M2	    3,148.0	  0.1		 7.4	7.8</p>
<p>    M3	    5,303.9	 -0.4		-0.2	0.4</p>
<p>    M4	    5,415.6	 -0.3		 0.2	0.9</p>
<p>Investment</p>
<p>    P1	    1,827.9	  0.8		18.4     18.3</p>
<p> Credit measure		billions	   Year-on-Year change</p>
<p>  (end-Aug)		    (unadj)	   Aug     July    June</p>
<p> Total domestic debt	10,926.6	   3.9     3.6	3.6</p>
<p> Total credits to economy  6,370.1	   0.1    -0.6	0.0</p>
<p> Bank credits to economy   3,571.3	   0.6    -0.7	0.3</p>
<p>The Bank originally said M3 money supply rose 0.6 percent in August, giving a year-on-year rise of 0.3 percent. It revised the August rise to 0.7 percent, giving a year-on-year rise of 0.4 percent.</p>
<p>The central bank is targeting M3 growth of roughly five percent a year on average over the next few years.</p>
<p>It is using total domestic debt as a secondary monitoring tool.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
